"<strong>Voltage divider.</strong> Use a {#} V source with \\(R_2 = 1.0\\ \\text{k}\\Omega\\) (the Voltage divider setup; its voltmeter V_out is across \\(R_2\\)). Take four \\(R_1\\) settings from approximately {#} to {#} kΩ: select R1 and set Resistance R to {#}, {#}, {#} and {#} kΩ, all on the slider. Measure \\(V_{\\rm out}\\) across \\(R_2\\) and the current (the setup has no ammeter: put one in the battery’s path first). Press Record reading at each setting. Keep the output unloaded.",
